"program_narrative": "Program BCHCTL00 is a batch control subprogram (incomplete in the delivered source) that is called with LS-CONTROL-REQUEST: a function code, job name, process date, sequence number and return code. It selects one action from the function code: INIT runs the initialisation sequence (open files, read control record, validate process, update start status), CHEK checks prerequisites, UPDT updates the process status in the control record, and TERM records completion and closes files; each action also sets an internal process-mode switch. All eleven worker paragraphs that would perform the file I/O on the indexed BATCH-CONTROL-FILE are missing from the source (listed only in a 'to be implemented' comment), so the actual reads and writes cannot be traced. The prerequisite check returns BCT-RC-SUCCESS (0) when prerequisites are satisfied and BCT-RC-WARNING (4) otherwise, but nothing in the present source sets the prerequisite flag. Error condition handled: an unknown function code sets the error text 'Invalid function code', return code BCT-RC-ERROR (8) and calls ERRPROC with ERR-MESSAGE. The program always copies LS-RETURN-CODE to RETURN-CODE and returns with GOBACK.",
